f3b5438a181aa3b6b372101eb55babff23","event_uuid":"13140549-1ca5-4418-abc9-b1b073a4f632","position":{"commit_sha":"32332b1afc9c509f4091c0cace66efef9f9572c8","position":"1787119913528765001-13140549-1ca5-4418-abc9-b1b073a4f632"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"038a75b928d1777924a11d398be69e65941de1d726b242146884be546d02c0ca","event_uuid":"c2045dec-c00e-4223-b5e7-a79aa66ee0dd","position":{"commit_sha":"9f5f4279f3b435fb0d2d1cd3a3a4b1c685624c8b","position":"1787120255819015001-c2045dec-c00e-4223-b5e7-a79aa66ee0dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"66589e1178666663a72a7187c5dcd65a98fb6699b5db17e574cab5c92821e4ea","event_uuid":"5502ca09-2e9e-4091-81aa-ebfd0c42fc8c","position":{"commit_sha":"6d20a950c2bd985cecb7a0ab460ac41cc2497b58","position":"1787120260567002001-5502ca09-2e9e-4091-81aa-ebfd0c42fc8c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-232_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"03a4b6e2-5666-42d5-8aaa-0906798afc8f","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC evidence (Gerrit 1892, landed as 9371328844, LLM-Review +1 + Verified +1, CI run 32219790927 success; 25 direct tests plus 3275 reconciler/interfaces tests green). AC1 at-most-one forward and matching reverse per transition -> every test calls a shared _assert_one_to_one helper that reloads both indexes FROM DISK and checks each reverse key points at a local id whose forward entry names that same key, plus no jira_key bound twice. AC2 bind_confirm stays last-writer-wins with exactly one targeted pop, no sweep/detection/abort -> test_bind_confirm_rebind_drops_only_the_differing_old_reverse_key and test_bind_confirm_rebind_does_not_sweep_an_out_of_band_orphan; the second was ADDED after mutation showed a sweep was indistinguishable in the first fixture, and it pins that an orphan the entry never named SURVIVES a rebind. AC3 stale reverse removal only in the permitted cases -> the two above plus test_unbind_clears_both_indexes_and_sweeps_orphans and test_unbind_of_a_keyless_entry_still_clears_its_reverse_key (the 874a regression: only the sweep can find a reverse key when the forward entry has no jira_key). AC4 immutable numeric-ID re-key instead of retiring -> test_rekey_swaps_both_indexes_and_resets_absence (asserts new key, absence reset to 0, jira_id unchanged, old reverse key gone) plus the facade-level test_facade_rekey_reports_a_move_and_updates_both_indexes returning True with no absence recorded. AC5 legacy no-ID records retain current behavior and facade signatures -> test_missing_numeric_id_reads_as_none_without_rewriting (and asserts the read does not rewrite the file), test_facade_rekey_degrades_to_absence_for_a_legacy_entry_with_no_numeric_id (whose fake client raises if consulted), and the parametrized test_facade_rekey_degrades_to_absence_without_a_usable_client covering both no-client and a client predating get_issue_by_rest. SEAM: note_absent_or_rekey stays on the facade as coordinator keeping the guard, the no-client/no-id fall-through and the by-id lookup; only the re-key mutation moved to BindingLifecycle.rekey, which declines on an empty or unchanged current key so both former note_absent branches collapse to one fall-through with NO outcome change. binding_store.py 710 -> 646 LOC; binding_lifecycle.py 229. _env_int and the RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE read deliberately did NOT move (they serve note_absent, which is T2 scope), and the implementer kept the non-literal env read on line 109 exactly so docs/env-vars.md stayed fresh. 6 defect-seeded mutations all RED.","timestamp":1787119913528765001}],"created_at":1787027525763725001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8985d76a-50fb-4865-9c72-78f7056faefd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3efd-36e0-fe91-405b"}],"description":"## Context\nAfter repository extraction, `BindingStore` still owns forward/reverse identity transitions, pending/confirmed state, stale reverse cleanup, and immutable numeric-ID moves. These coupled rules need one policy owner and both-index tests.\n\n## Outcome\nCreate the first `BindingLifecycle` slice for bind, confirm, unbind, reverse cleanup, and numeric-ID re-key while the public facade retains all signatures and owns coordination.\n\n## Plan\n1. Start with table-driven failing tests over valid, missing, corrupt, duplicate, and stale forward/reverse combinations.\n2. Move the cohesive identity transition call graph into `binding_lifecycle.py`, operating on repository-owned original dictionaries.\n3. Preserve the EXISTING behaviors exactly: targeted stale reverse removal (enumerated below), pending/confirmed semantics, immutable numeric-ID re-key, and legacy no-ID behavior. There is no ambiguity abort on the reviewed base and this slice does not introduce one.\n4. Delegate existing facade methods without exposing the lifecycle owner or repository to adapters.\n\n## Testing\nReload through the real repository after every transition and assert both indexes plus exact caller-visible outcomes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every valid bind/confirm/unbind transition leaves at most one forward and one matching reverse identity.\n- [x] `bind_confirm` remains last-writer-wins on the forward entry and pops EXACTLY the one differing old reverse key, with no sweep, no ambiguity detection, and no abort - the reviewed base has no such abort, so this slice must not add one.\n- [x] Stale reverse entries are removed only in the existing permitted cases.\n- [x] Immutable numeric-ID matches re-key moved issues instead of retiring them.\n- [x] Legacy records without numeric IDs retain current behavior and facade signatures.\n\n## Out of scope\nAbsence/tombstone/comment policy and rich-emission mutation move to later S2 tasks.\n\n## Extraction seam for `note_absent_or_rekey` (resolves the S2 T1 scope split)\n`note_absent_or_rekey` mixes this task's numeric-ID re-key rule with the absence/tombstone\npath that belongs to S2 T2, so the seam is named explicitly rather than left to the\nimplementer. On the reviewed base the method is:\n\n1. guard - resolve `local_id` + entry from the reverse index; return `False` if either is missing;\n2. no `client` or no captured `jira_id` -> `self.note_absent(jira_key)`; return `False`;\n3. `_current_key_by_id` returns nothing, or the same key -> `self.note_absent(jira_key)`; return `False`;\n4. a DIFFERENT current key -> re-key: set the entry's `jira_key`, reset `absent_404_count`, stamp\n   `updated_at`, pop the old reverse key, insert the new one, `save()`, emit `binding-rekeyed`.\n\nTHIS TASK extracts only step 4 (plus the step-3 identity comparison that decides it) into\n`binding_lifecycle.py` as a named re-key operation returning whether a re-key occurred.\n`note_absent_or_rekey` REMAINS on the facade as the coordinator: it asks the lifecycle owner\nto attempt a re-key and, on a negative result, falls through to `self.note_absent(...)`, which\nstays facade-owned until S2 T2 moves absence/retirement policy. The public signature and the\nTrue/False return contract do not change, and no branch changes its outcome - so\n`note_absent` is called in exactly the same cases, the same number of times, as before.\n\n## Permitted stale-reverse removals (enumerates AC3's \"existing permitted cases\")\nReverse entries may be removed ONLY in these existing cases; any other removal is a guessed\ndeletion and must safety-abort instead:\n- `bind_confirm` rebind: the entry already held a different `jira_key`, so the OLD key's\n  reverse entry is popped in the same operation (otherwise it dangles at this local id forever);\n- `unbind`: the keyed reverse entry is popped, then any reverse key still pointing at this\n  `local_id` is swept (this is the arm `bridge fsck --repair` prune relies on, including keys\n  orphaned out of band);\n- re-key (step 4 above): the old key is popped as the new key is inserted, in one operation;\n- `_retire`: the retired key's reverse entry is popped as the binding moves to the retired file.\n\n\n## Scope note: no ambiguity abort exists on the reviewed base (parent AC1 corrected to match)\nAn earlier draft of this task asserted an existing \"safety-abort on ambiguous double bind\" to be\npreserved. Verified against the code: none exists. `bind_confirm` unconditionally overwrites the\nforward entry's `jira_key`, then pops the old reverse key only when it differs; there is no\nambiguity detection, no refusal, and no raise. `unbind` and the re-key path likewise never abort.\n\nThe real invariant this task preserves is therefore NARROWER and is what the tests assert: every\ntransition leaves at most one forward entry and one matching reverse entry, achieved by targeted\nsingle-key pops rather than by detecting or refusing ambiguity. Adding an abort would be a\nBEHAVIOR CHANGE, which a pure extraction slice is forbidden from making; if an abort is wanted it\nbelongs in its own ticket with its own risk analysis. Parent story `brainy-cooked-hog` AC1 has been corrected to the same narrower invariant, so\nthe tree no longer contradicts itself. The term \"safety-abort\" is reserved for S3's\ninterrupted-retirement completion, which is genuinely new behavior there.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"New cohesive identity-transition policy owner."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Delegate identity operations behind the authoritative facade."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"Both-index transition and corruption tables."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py","reason":"Stale reverse cleanup regression coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py","reason":"Immutable-ID move and legacy signature oracles."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb"],["relates_to","3efd-36e0-fe91-405b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb","parent_status_uuid":"c2045dec-c00e-4223-b5e7-a79aa66ee0dd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp02","binding-lifecycle","tdd"],"ticket_id":"6083-b802-e90a-416e","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S2 T1 — Extract binding identity transitions","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Identity transitions, ambiguity, reverse cleanup, immutable-ID moves, and legacy compatibility"}]},"source_event_uuids":["5e1700c6-cc3b-4624-a15e-9b3d00eb4ede","1ec8acd3-72c9-4b69-bbd6-9e1720b47c6c","36081eb3-a87f-480d-8ba6-6811cc6b1d4d","728635b5-73aa-4910-a6a8-874221b500ff","825f71ab-c65e-4df0-a738-f1ff99303d19","ec116a28-b2a0-4d1a-9e73-4aeba563cea2","8985d76a-50fb-4865-9c72-78f7056faefd","13251f57-7a40-4d58-a931-9be0c3da2fa1","13140549-1ca5-4418-abc9-b1b073a4f632","c2045dec-c00e-4223-b5e7-a79aa66ee0dd","5502ca09-2e9e-4091-81aa-ebfd0c42fc8c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787123103389577001,"uuid":"08efe6dc-8a33-4a3a-8f74-0fffc573edb6"}